    <sys:String x:Key="Identity.Basis.NoReviewedWriteEvidence">M08: no reviewed, target-version evidence for modifying and restoring this field. Read-only. A successful observation neither implies write support nor determines VM identity on its own.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Identity.Basis.V02ExactRange">v0.2 tested only Workstation 17.5.2.23775571 / HW19 / two cores per socket, 4096↔6144 MiB and 2↔4 vCPU. Actual writes still require the existing policy and state checks.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Identity.Basis.M11MacExactRange">M11: Workstation 17 manual p.238; tested only on 17.5.2.23775571/vmrest1.3.1.23775571/HW19 with one static host-only NIC disconnected at startup. Existing MAC single-field apply, original-value restore and guest checks passed. Automatic-address conversion and multiple NICs remain unsupported. Actual writes require target, state, backup and concurrency checks plus explicit confirmation; declarations do not establish the effective MAC.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Identity.Basis.M11UuidExactRange">M11: Workstation 17 manual pp.160–161; tested only on 17.5.2.23775571/vmrest1.3.1.23775571/HW19 with one static host-only NIC disconnected at startup. Existing BIOS UUID single-field apply, original-value restore and guest checks passed. Missing keys and generation/copy workflows remain unsupported. Actual writes require target, state, backup and concurrency checks plus explicit confirmation; configuration restore excludes NVRAM and guest state.</sys:String>
