    <sys:String x:Key="IdentityConfig.Uuid">Replace existing BIOS UUID</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="IdentityConfig.Generate">Generate value and preview</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="IdentityConfig.Hidden">Hidden</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="IdentityConfig.Preview">New value preview generated; configuration has not changed. After review and confirmation, the official API must still verify version, power-off state, original content and backup before execution and independent result checks.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="IdentityConfig.ReviewOnly">Read-only preview generated. Identity writes are not approved for this version or target; commit is disabled and configuration has not changed.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="IdentityConfig.Unsupported">Cannot generate a candidate: requires hardware 19, existing VMware-format static MAC and BIOS UUID, and one host-only NIC disconnected at startup. Generated addresses, multiple NICs, encrypted or ambiguous configurations are unsupported.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="IdentityConfig.MacImpact">Changing MAC may affect DHCP, network rules and software bindings. Random values do not guarantee uniqueness across VMs. Only an existing static address is replaced; this does not hide VMware identity or change NIC connection or power.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="IdentityConfig.UuidImpact">Changing UUID may affect Windows, application licensing and asset bindings. Only an existing BIOS UUID is replaced; no copy or vendor-generation workflow runs, and other virtualization evidence remains.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="IdentityConfig.Reveal">Show this operation's original and new values locally</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="IdentityConfig.Privacy">Identity values are hidden by default and excluded from diagnostic exports and logs. Configuration backups and local recovery history contain original values and are private. A VMX backup restores configuration, not the whole VM.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="IdentityConfig.AcceptanceScope">Independent-copy candidate acceptance: only the target in this run's manifest is eligible. Backups and history are private test data. This candidate policy does not approve release writes; other targets remain ineligible.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="IdentityConfig.AcceptancePreview">Copy candidate generated. Review original/new values and effects. Confirmation still requires official API version, power, content, backup and independent result checks; no VM power operation is automatic.</sys:String>
